# PC-99: every text file is checked out with LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says.
# The licence files are hashed byte for byte (test/license.test.js), the release fixture is
# signed over its LF bytes (test/openpgp.test.js), and the tests that drive fake tools write
# shell scripts from the checkout, so a CRLF checkout on Windows would fail them.
* text=auto eol=lf
